        "original_id": "d92854ac-5c85-57f0-b734-a7bb42ce177b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Toyota Owners 400, Federated Auto Parts 400, Virginia 529 College Savings 250\n- Companies: Crown Royal, Diageo, Seagram\n- Places: Richmond Raceway, Richmond, Virginia, Daytona Speedweeks\n- Topics: NASCAR Cup Series, race sponsorship, essay contests\n\nFacts:\n- In 2000, Diageo acquired Crown Royal when the Seagram portfolio was dissolved.\n- Crown Royal is a blended Canadian whisky.\n- From 2007 to 2011, Crown Royal, a former title sponsor of the Toyota Owners 400, named the race after the winner of an essay contest held during Daytona Speedweeks.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is an annual Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series stock car race held at Richmond Raceway in Richmond, Virginia.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is the second of two Richmond Raceway Cup Series races, with the Toyota Owners 400 held in the spring as the first.\n- The Virginia 529 College Savings 250 is held on the night before the Federated Auto Parts 400.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
